#3_compile_and_merge_GPS_sources.R 

 
Setup  

 Use today's date in today_date. 

 Load new, old, and re-extracted survey data files. 

input: "/mnt/team/rapidresponse/pub/population/modeling/climate_malnutrition/input/extractions/dem_br/" 

compiled_old: use the last dataset compiled here  

reextracted: "/mnt/team/rapidresponse/pub/population/modeling/climate_malnutrition/input/extractions/dem_br/mort_rextractions/FILE" 

output:"/mnt/team/rapidresponse/pub/population/modeling/climate_malnutrition/input/extractions/dem_br/FILE"  

Cleaning 

Remove records corresponding to re-extracted NIDs from the main compiled dataset to avoid 

Duplication. We will add them back at the end. 

 Filter surveys likely to have GPS data based on known survey types (e.g., DHS, UNICEF_MICS, WHO, RHS) 

  

Geocodebook 

  

 Retrieve MBG (Model-Based Geostatistics) and SAE (Small Area Estimation) geocodebooks using NIDs present in the data. We prefer MBG for point data, but if unavailable see if it's in SAE. 

 

For surveys with both MBG and SAE geocodebooks: 

Prefer MBG if only point data is available or if MBG has specific administrative geomatching missing in SAE. 

Prefer SAE otherwise. 

Remove redundant geocodebook entries and combine into a single dataset. 

 Merge compiled survey data with geocodebook data using NID, location, and geospatial identifiers. 

  

 Final Cleaning 

Add back records for NIDs that required re-extractio 

Manual GPS File Merging for surveys where there was GPS files, but either it was not in the codebook correctly or not in the database at all. 

Remove surveys (by NID) that lack GPS information. 

Remove NIDs with missing age-at-death (aod_months) for deceased children. 

  

Quality Assurance 

 Summarize missingness of latitude and longitude per NID. 

Identify and export surveys with 100% missing GPS data for further review, using Records + NID tool from GHDx: https://internal-ghdx.healthdata.org/records-files-by-nid/ 

Filter out these surveys without GPS from final dataset. 

 Identify and report NIDs added or dropped compared to the previous compiled file. 

  

Output 

Export the cleaned and merged dataset to Parquet format. 

  

